A||||3||Homicidal||Replacing Dash Speakers||||1||
Z||000000||Homicidal||04-16-2000||12:18 PM||||Ordered some new 4X10's, how would I go about installing them?  Is it a simple "pop old one's out, put new one's in" deal, or do I need to rip apart my dash?<P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||04-16-2000||12:42 PM||||Is there a echo&gt;echo&gt;echo&gt;echo&gt; in here?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000002||Ed||04-16-2000||04:34 PM||||Just carefully pry up the screens with a flat bladed screwdriver.  Each screen is held in with four pressure fit thingy's (technical term). The speakers themselves are held in with four screws you can remove with a nut driver.   ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-16-2000||10:01 PM||||Radish rack(Radio Shack) part # 64-3058, I think, is a set of insulated crimps that fit most speaker terminals. <P>The way I did mine.... ((Which eliminates cutting the car wire harness.))<P>carefully remove the OEM terminals from the old speaker frame and clip the leads at the speaker cone.<P>Lay the terminals from both speakers the same side up, leads toward you, on a table. <P>Slide some plastic tubing on each of the leads.<P>Put a small crimp terminal on the left lead of each set. put a larger one on the right. (The size you use depends on your new speaker. It's usually the smallest and the middle sized ones.)<P>polarity from front to back doesn't matter as much as from left to right.<P>If you really want to insure polarity. ((Do this before cutting the harness off the old speakers.))<P>tape some wires to a AA or AAA battery. Connect + on the bat to + on the new speakers. tap the -'s together and watch wich way the speaker goes.<P>Now see which way the terminals on the old speaker are connected to make the cone move the same way as th new ones did when you tested them. Make the harness I described above keeping this in mind.||||reg||1
